// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Potentially Suspicious Regsvr32 HTTP/FTP Pattern
// Sigma ID: 867356ee-9352-41c9-a8f2-1be690d78216
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-24 | Modified: 2023-05-26
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.010
// Description: Detects regsvr32 execution to download/install/register new DLLs that are hosted on Web or FTP
//   servers.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/mrd0x/status/1461041276514623491
//   - https://twitter.com/tccontre18/status/1480950986650832903
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Regsvr32/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ad147b5514596e70f2782769d9833046b7c8e12b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_regsvr32_network_pattern.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\regsvr32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "REGSVR32.EXE") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " /i" or ProcessCommandLine contains " -i") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "ftp" or ProcessCommandLine contains "http")
